      "side": 1,
      "message": "Secure Connections is a defined term in the spec but non-Bluetooth folks may misunderstand it to mean something else.\nI wonder if we should say encryption algorithm here instead of just secure connections. Especially because this is about encryption rather than pairing.\n\nEncryption algorithm can be E0 or AES-CCM. E0 is only used by BR/EDR legacy and BR/EDR SSP pairing. BR/EDR secure connections, LE legacy and LE secure connections use AES-CCM.\n\n```\nint encryptionAlgorithm \u003d E0;     // BR/EDR legacy and SSP pairing\nif (secureConnections || transport \u003d TRANSPORT_LE) {\n  encryptionAlgorithm \u003d AES;   // BR/EDR secure connections and all LE pairing\n}\n```",
